	"title"            "Battle Cries — Character Voices"
	"description"      "[h1]Battle Cries[/h1]
Every character gets a voice. All 64 base characters have their own lines — a random battle-cry when a wave starts, plus an emote wheel to shout an emotion on demand during a run. Each character is voiced with its own personality and emotional delivery.

[h1]How to use[/h1]
[b]Wave start[/b] — automatic: your character shouts a random line each time a wave begins.
[b]Emote wheel[/b] — during a run, hold [b]T[/b] (keyboard) or [b]L2[/b] (controller), aim with the [b]mouse[/b] or the [b]right analog stick[/b], then release to play. Six emotions: Laugh, Cheer, Taunt, Nooo!, Hurt, Quip.
[b]Co-op[/b] — each player opens their own wheel with their own controller/keyboard and emotes with their own character. (The automatic wave-start bark is the leader's.)
[b]Turn it off[/b] — toggle the voices any time in [b]Settings > Audio > Character Voices[/b].

[h1]Notes[/h1]
[list]
[*]All 64 base characters are voiced.
[*]Voices are in English; on-screen labels follow the in-game language.
[*]The emote wheel only opens during a run, never in menus.
[/list]

[b]Tiếng Việt:[/b] Mỗi nhân vật có giọng nói riêng (đủ 64 nhân vật gốc). Đầu mỗi wave nhân vật tự hô một câu; trong trận giữ [b]T[/b] (bàn phím) hoặc [b]L2[/b] (tay cầm), ngắm bằng chuột hoặc cần analog phải rồi thả ra để phát cảm xúc. Chơi co-op: mỗi người dùng tay cầm/bàn phím của mình để mở bánh xe và emote bằng chính nhân vật của họ (câu hô đầu wave là của leader). Có thể bật/tắt giọng bất cứ lúc nào trong [b]Cài đặt > Âm Thanh[/b].

Requires Godot Mod Loader.

[h1]Source code / Contribute[/h1]
This mod is open source. Fork it, learn from it, or send a fix — the code is MIT and the mod's own art and audio are CC BY 4.0, so you are free to reuse and build on any of it as long as you credit the original.
[b]Repository:[/b] [url=https://github.com/hhoangg/brotato-battlecries]github.com/hhoangg/brotato-battlecries[/url]
Bug reports and ideas are welcome as GitHub issues, or as a comment here.

